@tradition rec-all-hands
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// The Captain's all-hands: the first Monday of each season, 17:45-18:10, the auditorium; Captain Marrow at the lectern,
// Commander Vance on the stage behind her; then everyone goes to dinner. The night shift sleeps and gets it in Mail
// (mail.rec.allhands.night). FOR RA: the first one is the Captain's address at the first ship-wide event (lead 17's call
// 1: no invented trigger), so Day 1 is skipped here (from day 2: the next is Day 92). A gathering.
k: 498
title: Captain's all-hands
when: quarter week 1 monday from day 2
at: 17:45-18:10
min: 20
prio: 2
where: 7 room Auditorium: rec:seat
hold: none
who: marrow always, vance always, night-shift never, officers 85%, everyone 70%
anim: everyone talk
host: marrow
from: marrow
flag: rec.on

== mail
- The Captain's all-hands is tomorrow, {time} in the auditorium. A new season, a few thanks, and then dinner. Everyone off duty, please come.

== ask
- All-hands before dinner. Comb your hair. The Captain notices. Well, Vance does.   #funny
- Coming to the all-hands? The Captain names a few people. You never know.

== here
- Shh. The Captain's on.
- Good turnout. She'll like that.

== thanks
- You find a seat as Captain Marrow steps to the lectern. Commander Vance stands behind her, very straight.

== chatter
- Did you hear the Captain at the all-hands? She named the whole galley.   #warm
- The Captain tapped the mic three times. Somebody fix the mic.   #funny
- I like the all-hands. It's short, and then there's dinner.   #funny
